---
import Component from "../../layouts/Component.astro"
import Anatomy from "../../components/Anatomy.astro"
import AutoExample from "../../components/AutoExample.astro"
import TabsBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/TabsBuild.astro"
import { Table, Tabs as UITabs } from "@opui/astro"

import TabsCSS from "@opui/css/components/tabs.css?raw"

import tabsItemApi from "../../component-api/tabs-item/api"
import tabsPanelApi from "../../component-api/tabs-panel/api"
import tabsTabApi from "../../component-api/tabs-tab/api"
import tabsApi from "../../component-api/tabs/api"
---

<Component
  slug="tabs"
  heroAnatomy
  apis={[
    { title: "Tabs API", api: tabsApi },
    { title: "Tabs item API", api: tabsItemApi },
    { title: "Tabs tab API", api: tabsTabApi },
    { title: "Tabs panel API", api: tabsPanelApi },
  ]}
  browserSupport={[
    "color-mix",
    "container-queries",
    "light-dark",
    "reading-flow",
    "scrollbar-width",
  ]}
  installationTabs={[{ title: "tabs.css", code: TabsCSS, lang: "css" }]}
  changelogPaths={[
    {
      path: "packages/opui/components/Tabs",
      type: "component",
    },
    { path: "src/docs/components/tabs.astro", type: "docs" },
    { path: "src/component-examples/tabs", type: "docs" },
    {
      path: "packages/opui/css/components/tabs.css",
      type: "css",
    },
    { path: "src/component-api/tabs", type: "api" },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Tabs</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="anatomy">
    <Anatomy>
      <UITabs name="tabs-anatomy">
        <UITabs.Item open>
          <UITabs.Tab>Profile</UITabs.Tab>
          <UITabs.Panel>Profile settings and information.</UITabs.Panel>
        </UITabs.Item>
        <UITabs.Item>
          <UITabs.Tab>Settings</UITabs.Tab>
          <UITabs.Panel>General account settings.</UITabs.Panel>
        </UITabs.Item>
      </UITabs>
    </Anatomy>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    The Tabs are radio inputs and the Panels are just divs that show and hide
    based on the radio inputs' <code>:checked</code> state.
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2 id="basics">Basics</h2>
    <AutoExample name="Basics" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="filled">Filled</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>variant="filled"</code> (<code>.ui-filled</code>) to fill the
      selected tab with the primary color.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Filled" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="line">Line</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>variant="line"</code> (<code>.ui-line</code>) for tabs without a
      background, marking the selected tab with a line.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Line" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="outlined">Outlined</h2>
    <p>
      Use <code>variant="outlined"</code> (<code>.ui-outlined</code>) for a
      bordered track without a background.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Outlined" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="scrollable">Scrollable</h2>
    <p>
      Tabs wrap onto more rows when they don't fit. Use <code>scrollable</code>
      {" "}(<code>.ui-scrollable</code>) to keep them on one row and scroll them
      sideways instead. The open panel stays in view, and up to 20 tabs are
      supported. The tabs size to their container, so give them a width inside
      flex and grid layouts that size to their content.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Scrollable" />
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="accessibility">
    <p>
      Tabs are radio buttons. Each tab is a radio input with a label, and the
      panel after it shows while it's checked. Screen readers announce a radio
      group ("Profile, radio button, checked, 1 of 3"), which matches how the
      tabs behave.
    </p>
    <p>
      There are no <code>tablist</code>, <code>tab</code> or
      {" "}<code>tabpanel</code> roles. ARIA tabs promise focusable tabs with a selected
      state, and radio inputs can't keep that promise without JavaScript. Native radios
      get group management and keyboard support for free.
    </p>
    <p>
      To name the group, add <code>role="radiogroup"</code> and
      {" "}<code>aria-label</code> (or <code>aria-labelledby</code>) to
      {" "}<code>.ui-tabs</code>.
    </p>

    <Table>
      <Table.ColumnGroup>
        <Table.Column width="150px" />
        <Table.Column width="150px" />
        <Table.Column />
      </Table.ColumnGroup>
      <Table.Head>
        <Table.Row>
          <Table.HeaderCell>Element</Table.HeaderCell>
          <Table.HeaderCell>Attribute</Table.HeaderCell>
          <Table.HeaderCell>Description</Table.HeaderCell>
        </Table.Row>
      </Table.Head>
      <Table.Body>
        <Table.Row>
          <Table.Cell><code>input</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell><code>name</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell
            >Groups the radio buttons together for exclusive selection.</Table.Cell
          >
        </Table.Row>
        <Table.Row>
          <Table.Cell><code>input</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell><code>checked</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell>Selects the tab that is open initially.</Table.Cell>
        </Table.Row>
        <Table.Row>
          <Table.Cell><code>label</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell><code>for</code></Table.Cell>
          <Table.Cell>Names the radio button after the tab.</Table.Cell>
        </Table.Row>
      </Table.Body>
    </Table>

    <h3>Keyboard Interaction</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Tab</strong>: Moves focus to the active tab trigger (the radio
        button). Pressing Tab again moves focus out of the tabs to the next
        focusable element.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right Arrow / Down Arrow</strong>: Moves focus to the next tab
        and activates it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Left Arrow / Up Arrow</strong>: Moves focus to the previous tab
        and activates it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
  <TabsBuild slot="under-the-hood" />
</Component>
